      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 60 year-old Japanese man having a 20-year history of diabetes mellitus presented with truncal neuropathy. The severe pain, especially its nocturnal exacerbation, prevented him from sleeping and eating, resulting in rapid emaciation. However, he recovered from the condition with oral mexiletine, which dramatically controlled the pain."},
